The check of Paul Zimmermann's tables for k = 9, l = 6.

The whole archive (687184 lines in 2203 files in<e>, one per binade
[2^(e-1), 2^e) of exp x) is all.tar.bz2, sha256
f509e74ec47064ede889eea481decf2a8f8f7a57fcba875796bd17413e58b85e, from
Paul (filesender).  sample.tar.xz holds 22 of its files, 7136 lines.

  tar xJf sample.tar.xz
  ./mksample.sh in1024 in1023 in1000 in900 in700 in500 in300 in100 in10 \
     in2 in1-0 in0-0 in-1 in-100 in-500 in-900 in-1000 in-1021 in-1022 \
     in-1023 in-1050 in-1074
  make -j15 sample
  make sample-all        # SampleAll.v: the theorem, one lemma per file
                         # AllCover.v: the coverage, one theorem per run

mksample.sh also writes Cover_N.v, the check (ExpCover.contig, parsing
only) that the lines of a file follow each other: each line starts at the
double right after the last double x0 + n u of the previous one, also
when x crosses a binade.  It orders the files by their first x0 and cuts
them into maximal runs of files that follow each other (ExpCover.joins);
it reports on stderr the files that do not join, and leaves out of the
runs the files whose lines do not follow each other.  AllCover.v has one
theorem coverK per run: every normal double y = S 2^(ex - 52) between the
first x0 and the last x1 of the run is x0 + j u, 0 <= j <= n, in a line
whose text satisfies the six conditions.  On the whole archive there are
two runs, from -0x1.74910d52d3051p+9 to -0x1.0000000000001p-53 and from
0x1p-53 to 0x1.62e42fefa39efp+9 (the end of a run is x0 + n u of its last
line); the doubles strictly between them, around 0, are in no table.

E = 0x600001 * 2^320 is inferred from the data (every line keeps the
rounding term and the Taylor term below 2^-43), not read from Paul's
program.

The whole archive is in archive/, as five parts tables0..4.tar.bz2 (under
100 MB each, the size GitHub accepts), with their SHA256SUMS; together they
hold exactly the 2203 files of Paul's all.tar.bz2.  Then

  ulimit -s unlimited
  ./fullrun.sh 20 2>&1 | tee full.log

checks the parts, unpacks them into tables/, writes one Data_N.v,
Run_N.v and Cover_N.v per file, runs them with 20 workers and builds
SampleAll.v and AllCover.v over all the files.
